{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/device/device_plugins.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:28:47.146560Z","id":"c3f4359f0f69de4a846e85e9cbba4b97ca41c21f770b13494fbfdcc19bfecc15","body":{"detail":"test/platform/device/device_host_test.dart and test/ui/app_screen_device_test.dart drive DeviceHost through fake ports; nothing has run PluginNotifier, PluginShare, PluginFiles, PluginCamera or PluginLocation on Android or macOS. `flutter build apk --debug --target-platform android-arm64` compiles and the merged manifest carries ScheduledNotificationReceiver, ScheduledNotificationBootReceiver and the location permissions. Unchecked: (1) zonedSchedule with AndroidScheduleMode.inexactAllowWhileIdle fires near its time, repeats daily and weekly (DateTimeComponents.time / dayOfWeekAndTime), and survives a reboot; a force stop clears Android's alarms while device-reminders.json still lists them (Reminders.list, reminders.dart:177); (2) a tap on a reminder reaches onDidReceiveNotificationResponse while running and getNotificationAppLaunchDetails from cold, and app.dart's _onReminderTap brings the app up and runs claxHost.openRoute once its page is ready, moving the frame by popstate; (3) image_picker's camera intent works without the CAMERA permission and maxWidth/maxHeight 1600 downscale, and ImageDescriptor reads the size; (4) FilePicker.pickFile / saveFile and SharePlus on Android 10+; (5) geolocator's permission flow and 20 s time limit; (6) on macOS (sandbox, com.apple.security.files.user-selected.read-write added) the notification permission prompt, file and photo pickers, and share; location and camera.take answer unavailable there. Also unmeasured: a 10 MB file goes to the page as about 13 MB of base64 inside one runJavaScript string (host_protocol.dart DeviceResult.toJs).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":21},"end":{"line":245},"content_hash":"b99b8da202734d1b2dc6eacea5081ba8796aaec6a553b75447c0b024bcd5f241"},"summary":"The device capabilities' plugin ports are unverified on a device: reminders, a reminder's tap, share, file pick and save, camera and location have only fake-port tests","tags":["v1","unverified","device","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/device/device_host.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:28:47.146792Z","id":"0556ac93b7d57e833328c9a62e0455b6283e1758506b400d2f4b70371f243a6e","body":{"detail":"DeviceHost._allow (device_host.dart:187) checks only the stored grant; neither the shell (web/shell/src/caps/device.ts) nor the app requires a recent gesture in the page, unlike comments and artifact.publish (caps/gesture.ts). A granted app can call location.current() in a loop or open the camera on load. A Don't allow is kept only in memory (_refused, line 53), so after an app restart the page may ask again on every launch.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":187},"end":{"line":206},"content_hash":"ca708015e3bd8b3cd75b41f38d9c6af166bda045ef6805ecccc3c0a307250cee"},"suggested_fix":"Require the viewer's gesture (the shell's frameGesture rule) for camera, files, share and location calls, and keep a refusal in DeviceGrants until the person changes it in the app inspector.","summary":"Once a device capability is allowed, the page can open the camera, a picker or the share sheet, or read location, without the person's tap","tags":["v1","security","device","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/device/device_host.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:32:07.708948Z","id":"81ede8920760672ac146c5198d06ea44f1dc1b0506daa24a13effd9faa5c8b93","body":{"detail":"Failure: allow camera or location for any app, then open its inspector's Permissions: the Device row is the plannedPermissionKinds placeholder (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_inspector_permissions.dart:86), no PermissionSource of kind `device` exists, and `grep -rn '\\.revoke(' apps/clax_app/lib` finds no caller of DeviceHost.revoke. The consent dialog (device_consent_dialog.dart:52) and contract C5 (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-real-apps-design.md) promise the grant is kept until revoked in the app inspector, so an Allow is irrevocable short of clearing the app's data, and reminders of a revoked notify grant are never cancelled.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":80},"end":{"line":85},"content_hash":"68b1bb52f3bda987fde1b638b5403449822cd4bf62775476cbf8d796ee3dadda"},"suggested_fix":"Add a `device` PermissionSource listing DeviceGrants.list(aid) with a Revoke calling DeviceHost.revoke, passed to the inspector from AppRoot.","summary":"No surface revokes a device grant: DeviceHost.revoke has no caller, and the app inspector shows Device as still to come","tags":["v1-review","security","device","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/device/device_host.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:32:07.709049Z","id":"1e0432d4048b960815ab10799b9281aad419758ddd64b546835ec54f4af87a67","body":{"detail":"Prompt-level consent alone lets a granted page read location.current() silently at every load, and a page that calls on load re-asks after every restart (_refused at device_host.dart:53 is memory only), so the person is nagged on each launch. The cheapest safe rule: in deviceHandler (web/shell/src/caps/device.ts) reject with CapError('no_gesture') unless frameGesture() (web/shell/src/caps/gesture.ts:548, already fed by attestPointer in the app) holds, for share, files, camera, location and notify.schedule; and store a refusal next to the grant, cleared by the inspector's revoke (needs the device PermissionSource first). With the gesture rule a re-ask can only follow a tap, which bounds the nag even before the refusal is persisted.","kind":"comment","references":"0556ac93b7d57e833328c9a62e0455b6283e1758506b400d2f4b70371f243a6e","summary":"Recommended rule: frameGesture() in the shell for every device call except notify.list and notify.cancel; persist Don't allow in DeviceGrants","tags":["v1-review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/device/device_host.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:32:07.709169Z","id":"e302b248190c6d0516c54e3df5d2747a3cb2daeb760dc774baaa76ca601e1904","body":{"detail":"files.pick returns up to 13.4 MB of base64 inside the runJavaScript source (DeviceResult.toJs, host_protocol.dart:541, JSON-encoded then jsString-escaped), which the shell JSON.parses and then postMessages into the frame; share.file and files.save carry the same size the other way through the JavaScript channel. On a mid-range Android WebView that is tens of MB of UTF-16 copies and a multi-second main-thread stall; untested on a device (c3f4359f).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":21},"end":{"line":21},"content_hash":"f2c0bd2430a2205e01d61ca17635e46d91c086b32bebd79cfb7a7f0cdc9d13ea"},"suggested_fix":"Cap at 4 MB for the prototype (camera results are already downscaled to 1600 px), and test one maximal pick on a device.","summary":"10 MB of base64 crosses the channel as one JavaScript string, several copies deep","tags":["v1-review","device","perf","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/lib/platform/device/reminders.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:32:07.709204Z","id":"59d989289fdb157f3528cdb73165aca8e1fe3cfd0530664ba4fb6fd3e2470b98","body":{"detail":"Nothing calls cancelAll on artifact_deleted, so a deleted app's reminders fire and their tap opens an app that is gone. _check (line 206) bounds each reminder but not their number: every weekly reminder takes one native alarm per weekday, and Android refuses an app's alarms past 500, after which every app's notify.schedule fails as unavailable.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":199},"end":{"line":205},"content_hash":"f1357d3f6538bbca660760d46071099eb9d737ee68b19a67d0a695589ee6d3bc"},"suggested_fix":"Cancel an app's reminders on artifact_deleted (AppRoot sees the gallery events); cap reminders per app (e.g. 64) with a too_many error.","summary":"A deleted app's reminders keep firing, and a page may schedule without a count limit","tags":["v1-review","device","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
